.TH HSH 1 "August 2026" "0.1" "Simple Shell Manual"
.SH NAME
hsh \- Simple UNIX command interpreter
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ./hsh
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B hsh
is a simple UNIX command language interpreter that reads commands from either standard input or from a file and executes them.
.PP
The shell can be used interactively and non-interactively. In interactive mode, it displays a prompt \fB($)\fR and waits for the user to input commands. In non-interactive mode, it reads commands from pipes or files without printing a prompt.

.SH INVOCATION
To run \fBhsh\fR interactively:
.IP
.B ./hsh

To run \fBhsh\fR non-interactively:
.IP
.B echo "/bin/ls" | ./hsh

.SH BUILTINS
The shell supports the following built-in commands:
.TP
.B exit
Exits the shell.
.TP
.B env
Prints the current environment variables.

.SH RETURN VALUE
Upon successful execution of a command, \fBhsh\fR returns the exit status of the last command executed. If an error occurs, an error message is printed to standard error and a non-zero exit status is returned.

